---
/**
 * TEACHING & LEARNING · SMART CLASSROOMS & DIGITAL LITERACY — audit §2C.
 *
 * ⚠ THE BANNER IS THE SHARED PageHero AND ITS TREATMENT IS UNTOUCHED — same
 * component, same photograph, same crop, same crumbs, same height, same title
 * and standfirst as before and as every other Academics page. All of the
 * redesign is below it.
 *
 * ⚠ COMBINED PAGE — two of the brief's fourteen bullets: Smart Classrooms and
 * AI & Digital Literacy. The standalone /ai-digital-literacy/ route was an
 * implementation experiment; its verified content is merged here and the route
 * is retired.
 *
 * The page was rebuilt off the generic AcSplit → AcCollage → AcStatement →
 * AcClose system into a composed one: five sections that tell a single story —
 * the room, the infrastructure, the point of it, the practice, what is still
 * changing. Everything below the banner lives in
 * components/academics/teaching/SmartClassroomsPage.astro, and that file's
 * frontmatter carries every figure's source and the standing warning about the
 * one number on this page that has been published wrong before.
 *
 * ⚠ SCOPE BOUNDARY — the METHOD that runs on this equipment is Teaching
 * Methodology's; the Robotics Lab and the national science programmes are STEM,
 * Robotics & Enrichment's. This page is the room and the subject.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import SmartClassroomsPage from '../../../components/academics/teaching/SmartClassroomsPage.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/computer lab/DSC_1204 copy.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={banner}
  />

  {/* ⚠ THE PANEL IS REQUIRED. PageHero is sticky and this panel covers it as the
      page scrolls; without it the banner hangs under the footer.

      ⚠ AND THE PADDING RESET IS AN INLINE STYLE, DELIBERATELY. `.u-page-panel`
      in base.css carries `padding-bottom: var(--sb-section-y)` — 120px of empty
      cream between the closing section and the footer. A stylesheet form of the
      override can be served from a different build than the HTML that needs it,
      and then it silently stops applying; an inline style travels IN the HTML,
      so the two cannot skew. Same decision as the other redesigned pages. */}
  <div class="u-page-panel" style="padding-block: 0;">
    <SmartClassroomsPage />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
